; claude: money as a person keeps it (TinyQuicken, apps/pim/): amounts
; in whole cents (Money), the register of a checking account and what
; it remembers (Ledger), balancing it against the bank's statement
; (Reconcile), and the file every personal finance program exchanged
; (Qif). The dates are core's Civil.
;
; Pure OCaml, no gui, no playground: in the package tiny_appkits, as
; tiny_appkits.appkit_money, so every backend, the web one included,
; can use it; tested without a screen in appkits/tests/.
(library
 (name appkit_money)
 (public_name tiny_appkits.appkit_money)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries elm_core)
)
